{"task_id": "HumanEval/62", "solution": "class InvalidPolynomialError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid polynomial input.\"\"\"\n    pass\ndef derivative(xs: list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the derivative of a polynomial given its coefficients.\n    Returns a list representing the coefficients of the derivative.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(xs, list):\n        raise InvalidPolynomialError(\"Input must be a list of coefficients.\")\n\n    if not all(isinstance(c, (int, float)) for c in xs):\n        raise InvalidPolynomialError(\"All coefficients must be numeric (int or float).\")\n\n    if not xs or len(xs) == 1:\n        return []\n\n    derivative_coefficients = []\n    for i in range(1, len(xs)):\n        derivative_coefficients.append(xs[i] * i)\n\n    return derivative_coefficients"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/61", "solution": "def correct_bracketing(brackets: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\" brackets is a string of \"(\" and \")\".\n    return True if every opening bracket has a corresponding closing bracket.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(brackets, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n\n    # A list is used as a stack to track opening brackets.\n    stack = []\n    for char in brackets:\n        if char == '(':\n            stack.append(char)\n        elif char == ')':\n            if not stack:\n                return False\n            stack.pop()\n    return not stack"}
